==English==

===Etymology===
English form of {{L.}} [[Aemilia]], a [[w:gens|gens]] name from ''aemulus'' "[[rival]]" or "those in the next valley". In medieval England it was sometimes interchangeable with Germanic [[Amelia]].

===Proper noun===
'''Emily''' (''plural'' '''Emilys'''<!--this is correct-->)

a person who is very gullible. and retarded.

